          alt: "Three curves showing where the mean, median and mode sit. Symmetrical: mean equals median equals mode, all at the peak — use the mean. Positive skew: mode less than median less than mean, tail to the right, a few very high values pull the mean up — use the median. Negative skew: mean less than median less than mode, tail to the left — use the median. The skew is named after the tail, not the hump, and the mean always chases the tail, which is why outliers make it lie.",
          caption: "Length of stay, household income and the number of children per woman are all skewed to the right — a few very large values drag the mean up, so the median is the honest average.",
