            "<strong>One Health</strong> recognises that most emerging infections are zoonoses — anthrax in cattle and the people who butcher them in the Upper East, rabies from unvaccinated dogs, avian influenza in poultry farms, Lassa fever from rodents, Marburg and Ebola from bats and bushmeat — and that human health, animal health and environmental services must share surveillance and respond together. In practice the nurse reports clusters of dead or sick animals as readily as sick people, works with the veterinary officer on dog-bite follow-up and ring vaccination of animals, and tells the community not to eat an animal that died of unknown cause.",
